.TH "VIRTUALBRICKS\-MIGRATE" "1" "2026\-10\-24" "virtualbricks 3.0.0.dev8" "Virtualbricks Manual"
.SH NAME
virtualbricks\-migrate \- convert the files of Virtualbricks 2.1 and
older
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]virtualbricks\-migrate\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-in\-place\f[R]]
[\f[B]\-\-settings\f[R] \f[I]file\f[R]] [\f[I]input\f[R]
[\f[I]output\f[R]]]
.PP
\f[B]python \-m virtualbricks.migrate\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-settings\f[R]
\f[I]file\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-copy\-files\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]]
[\f[B]\-v\f[R]] \f[I]input\f[R] \f[I]output\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]python \-m virtualbricks.migrate \-\-in\-place\f[R]
[\f[B]\-\-settings\f[R] \f[I]file\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]]
[\f[B]\-v\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Virtualbricks 2.1 and older kept their settings in
\f[I]\(ti/.virtualbricks.conf\f[R] and each project in a
\f[I].project\f[R] file; this version reads the files of
\f[B]virtualbricks\-config\f[R](5).
The migration converts the old files into the new ones, as Virtualbricks
does by itself the first time it starts after an upgrade.
The old files are only read; what the conversion does to each setting,
brick and event is in the MIGRATION section of
\f[B]virtualbricks\-config\f[R](5).
.PP
\f[B]virtualbricks\-migrate\f[R] opens the window of the migration,
filled with what it\(aqs given: the old workspace, \f[I]input\f[R], and
the folder to write into, \f[I]output\f[R], or with
\f[B]\-\-in\-place\f[R] the files of the user.
The window shows what it converted, project by project.
.PP
\f[B]python \-m virtualbricks.migrate\f[R] does the same without the
window, and prints what it converted.
Given an old workspace and a new or empty folder, it writes into the
folder, laid out like the XDG directories, to try the migration out on
copies:
.TP
\f[I]output\f[R]/config/virtualbricks/settings.toml
The settings, from the file of \f[B]\-\-settings\f[R].
.TP
\f[I]output\f[R]/state/virtualbricks/state.toml
The state, with the project that was open last in the file of
\f[B]\-\-settings\f[R].
.TP
\f[I]output\f[R]/workspace/\f[I]project\f[R]/project.toml
Each project, with its README if it has one.
.TP
\f[I]output\f[R]/migration\-report.txt
What it converted, as it printed it.
.PP
Given \f[B]\-\-in\-place\f[R], it migrates the files of the user: the
settings and the state go into the XDG directories, and the
\f[B]project.toml\f[R] of each project next to its \f[I].project\f[R]
file, in the workspace that the old settings name.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-gui\f[R]
Open the window of the migration, as \f[B]virtualbricks\-migrate\f[R]
does.
\f[B]\-\-copy\-files\f[R], \f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R] and
\f[B]\-\-verbose\f[R] aren\(aqt available there.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-in\-place\f[R]
Migrate the files of the user, next to the old ones.
It takes no folders.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-settings\f[R] \f[I]file\f[R]
An old settings file to migrate too.
With \f[B]\-\-in\-place\f[R], it\(aqs \f[I]\(ti/.virtualbricks.conf\f[R]
if there is one, unless this names another.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-copy\-files\f[R]
Copy the disks and the other files of each project into \f[I]output\f[R]
too; without it, only the converted files and the README are written.
It\(aqs for a migration into a folder.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]
Convert and check everything, but write nothing.
.TP
\f[B]\-v\f[R], \f[B]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Print the informational messages too, beside the warnings and the
errors.
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\-\-help\f[R]
Print the options, then exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Every project was migrated; warnings are fine.
\f[B]virtualbricks\-migrate\f[R] ends with 0 once its window closes.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
A project failed.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
The arguments are wrong.
.TP
\f[B]3\f[R]
Virtualbricks is running, and the files are to be migrated in place:
close it first.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]\(ti/.virtualbricks.conf\f[R]
The settings of Virtualbricks 2.1 and older, which
\f[B]\-\-in\-place\f[R] migrates.
.TP
\f[I]workspace\f[R]/\f[I]project\f[R]/.project
A project of Virtualbricks 2.1 and older.
.TP
\f[I]$XDG_STATE_HOME\f[R]/virtualbricks/migration\-report.txt
What the migration in place converted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Try the migration on copies, then read what it did:
.IP
.EX
python \-m virtualbricks.migrate \(rs
    \-\-settings \(ti/.virtualbricks.conf \(ti/vb\-copy /tmp/vb\-test
less /tmp/vb\-test/migration\-report.txt
.EE
.PP
Check the files of the user, then migrate them:
.IP
.EX
python \-m virtualbricks.migrate \-\-in\-place \-\-dry\-run
python \-m virtualbricks.migrate \-\-in\-place
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]virtualbricks\f[R](1), \f[B]virtualbricks\-config\f[R](5)
